{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Ceups4Qr1NaYJV7Rv7gtg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I have a clear picture of the codebase. Let me summarize my findings:\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that manages order cancellation with ACTIVE/CANCELLED status, idempotent retry behavior, validation against confirmed shipments, and prevention of shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity at Order.kt:11-16 has no status field\n- OrderController.kt:21-46 shows the current API pattern\n- Shipment.kt:23-27 has ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController.kt:26-44 creates shipments\n- ApiExceptions.kt:11-24 defines the exception hierarchy\n- ApiError.kt:31-37 defines ErrorCode enum\n- GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28 handles exceptions centrally\n\n**Conventions in this repo:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409)\n- Tests validate error envelope shape: `$.error.code` and `$.error.message`\n- Repositories use in-memory ConcurrentHashMap stores\n- POST endpoints return 201 CREATED with `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body()`\n- Tests use `@BeforeEach` to clear repository state\n- One error code per scenario in ErrorCode enum\n\n**Affected files and why:**\n1. Order.kt - Must add OrderStatus enum and status field\n2. OrderRepository.kt - Must add method to find shipments by orderId for validation\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt - Must add method to find shipments by orderId for cancel operation\n4. OrderController.kt - Must add cancel endpoint\n5. ShipmentController.kt - Must validate order isn't cancelled before accepting shipment\n6. ApiError.kt - Must add ORDER_ALREADY_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT error codes\n7. OrderControllerTest.kt - Must add cancel tests\n\n**Risks:**\n- If order doesn't exist, 404 must be returned (ResourceNotFoundException handles this)\n- Concurrent cancellation attempts require idempotent semantics\n- Partial state changes (some shipments cancelled, some not) must be prevented when confirmed shipment exists\n- ShipmentController needs access to OrderRepository to validate order status\n\n**Open questions:** None that require escalation.\n\nNow I'll proceed to design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values. Add `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field to Order data class. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** - No changes needed; the repository operations remain unchanged. Saving an order updates its status in place.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to query all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if order doesn't exist\n   - Throws ConflictException with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT if any shipment is CONFIRMED\n   - If order is CANCELLED, succeeds without changes (idempotent)\n   - Otherwise, sets order status to CANCELLED and cancels all CREATED shipments\n   - Returns the cancelled order with 200 OK\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - Inject OrderRepository and in the create endpoint, check if the order exists and is not CANCELLED. If cancelled, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED error code. Non-existent orders proceed as before (current behavior preserved).\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** - Add two error codes:\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` - When cancel is blocked by confirmed shipment\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` - When creating shipment for cancelled order\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests:\n   - Cancel active order succeeds, returns order with CANCELLED status, and cancels CREATED shipments\n   - Cancel already-cancelled order succeeds without changes (idempotent)\n   - Cancel order with confirmed shipment returns 409, changes nothing\n   - Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add test:\n   - Creating shipment for cancelled order returns 409\n\n**Alternative rejected and why:**\n- Alternative: Track cancellation in a separate field instead of changing status. Rejected because: (1) status field is clearer semantically, (2) consistent with ShipmentStatus pattern, (3) easier to query in tests.\n- Alternative: Use a service layer to encapsulate cancel logic. Rejected because: (1) no service layer exists in current architecture, (2) would violate \"no unrelated refactoring\" constraint, (3) controller can handle the logic directly given in-memory data.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel Active Order (Happy Path):**\n   - Input: `POST /orders/O-1/cancel`\n   - Validate: Order exists\n   - Validate: No CONFIRMED shipments\n   - Action: Set order.status = CANCELLED; for each CREATED shipment, set status = CANCELLED\n   - Persist: Save order; save each cancelled shipment\n   - Output: 200 OK, order with CANCELLED status\n\n2. **Cancel Already-Cancelled Order (Idempotent):**\n   - Input: `POST /orders/O-1/cancel` (where O-1 is already CANCELLED)\n   - Validate: Order exists\n   - Action: No-op (order already CANCELLED)\n   - Output: 200 OK, order with CANCELLED status\n\n3. **Cancel with Confirmed Shipment (All-or-nothing):**\n   - Input: `POST /orders/O-1/cancel` (with CONFIRMED shipment)\n   - Validate: Order exists\n   - Validate: Check shipments; find one with status CONFIRMED\n   - Action: Abort; throw ConflictException\n   - Persist: No changes to any entity\n   - Output: 409 CONFLICT, error envelope with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT\n\n4. **Cancel Non-existent Order:**\n   - Input: `POST /orders/O-missing/cancel`\n   - Validate: Order doesn't exist\n   - Output: 404 NOT_FOUND, error envelope with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n\n5. **Create Shipment for Cancelled Order:**\n   - Input: `POST /shipments` with orderId for CANCELLED order\n   - Validate: Order exists\n   - Validate: Order is not CANCELLED\n   - Action: Abort; throw ConflictException\n   - Output: 409 CONFLICT, error envelope with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n6. **Create Shipment for Non-existent Order:**\n   - Input: `POST /shipments` with non-existent orderId\n   - Current behavior: Allows creation (order validation happens elsewhere or not at all)\n   - New behavior: Still allows creation (unchanged; ticket says \"keeps its current behaviour\")\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nNew tests in OrderControllerTest:\n- `cancel_active_order_succeeds_and_cancels_created_shipments` - Create order, create CREATED shipment, cancel, verify order is CANCELLED and shipment is CANCELLED, response is 200\n- `cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds_idempotently` - Create and cancel order, cancel again, verify same state, response is 200\n- `cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment_returns_409_and_changes_nothing` - Create order, create shipment, manually set to CONFIRMED (via repository), cancel, verify 409 with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT, verify order still ACTIVE, shipment still CONFIRMED\n- `cancel_non_existent_order_returns_404` - Try to cancel non-existent order, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n\nNew test in ShipmentControllerTest:\n- `creating_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409` - Create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\nAll tests validate both status code and error envelope structure (error.code, error.message).\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":894,"cache_read_input_tokens":19717,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":894},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":